BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:13th Annual Stone Skipping Festival
DTSTART:20260919T130000
DTEND:20260919T190000
DTSTAMP:20260919T143151Z
UID:369852f8e82a5331d3759491083fff@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:STONES WILL FLY Lake Paran Community Center’s Stone Skipping
  Festival Returns September 19 from 1-7PM NORTH BENNINGTON\, VT — Some p
 eople spend their Saturdays doing sensible things. On Saturday\, September
  19\, 2026\, Lake Paran Community Center will be encouraging people to thr
 ow rocks at a lake. Lake Paran is a community hub in North Bennington\, Ve
 rmont\, where people gather to enjoy the outdoors\, spend time on the wate
 r\, and occasionally discover that a flat rock can be surprisingly enterta
 ining. Come join the Guiness Book of World Records holder\, Kurt Steiner a
 nd others from around the country as they compete for the trophy at Lake P
 aran. Here are 2 videos to give you a better idea of how amazing this even
 t really is: https://www.youtube.com/shorts/J5OcfD0iBIU https://www.outsid
 eonline.com/outdoor-adventure/water-activities/stone-skipping-kurt-steiner
 / Lake Paran Community Center’s 13th Annual Stone Skipping Festival will
  take place from 1:00 to 7:00 p.m.\, bringing together stone-skipping enth
 usiasts\, curious spectators\, live music\, and anyone who has ever looked
  at a lake and thought\, “I bet I can make that rock bounce.” Some peo
 ple can skip it once\, while others can skip it clear across the lake! You
  have to see it to believe it. Guests can enjoy an afternoon of stone-skip
 ping action along with food trucks serving up festival fare and live music
  from the Olson Brothers Band. And yes\, we sell perfect stones for you to
  skip! There is a small fee to compete\, it’s free to come watch and enj
 oy the show. We always appreciate your donation. Whether you are a seasone
 d stone skipper with a finely honed technique or someone who has never suc
 cessfully gotten a rock to bounce even once\, Lake Paran invites you to co
 me out and give it a try. There will be impressive skips. There will be sp
 ectacular kerplunks. There will be cries of disbelief as stones skip grace
 fully across the water over 50 times. So mark your calendar\, bring your f
 riends\, and prepare yourself for an afternoon dedicated to one of humanit
 y’s oldest and least necessary pastimes. EVENT DETAILS What: Lake Paran 
 Stone Skipping Festival Cost: Free entry\, donation suggested. Amateur reg
 istration $5.00 to compete When: Saturday\, September 19\, 2026\, 1:00–7
 :00 p.m. Where: Lake Paran\, North Bennington\, Vermont Featuring: Stone s
 kipping\, food trucks\, live music For more information\, visit www.lakepa
 ranvt.org or our Facebook page for updates\, https://www.facebook.com/lake
 paran/\n\nSources: Vermont Public
LOCATION:Lake Paran\, 269 Houghton St.
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/13th-annua
 l-stone-skipping-festival-08-09-2026-06-48-53
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
