BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Burlington Baroque Festival: Boston's Blue Heron
DTSTART:20260919T140000
DTEND:20260919T153000
DTSTAMP:20260919T143151Z
UID:da55ea1b77c0f241594c5f3a4db7c4@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:Boston's critically acclaimed ensemble Blue Heron (Scott Metca
 lfe\, Artistic Director) presents an extraordinary program of 15th-century
  Franco-Flemish chansons and the sacred motets and masses that borrow thei
 r secular tunes. Divine Songs: Secular Chansons & Sacred Transformations\,
  features music by Binchois\, DuFay\, Ockeghem\, Agricola\, LaRue\, and Ba
 uldeweyn\, who were among the most celebrated and distinguished composers 
 of the Renaissance. Scott Metcalfe and his team of extraordinary artists h
 ave been leaders in the field in bringing this repertoire to world audienc
 es through their many critically acclaimed recordings\, numerous tours\, a
 nd their resident series in Cambridge. This will be a rare opportunity for
  our region to enjoy a precious repertoire presented by one of the most ac
 claimed ensembles in the world of early music. We are delighted to bring B
 lue Heron to the 2026 Burlington Baroque Festival and to welcome back Burl
 ingtonian Scott Metcalfe! Blue Heron Artists: Kim Leeds\, Sophie Michaux\,
  Sonja DuToit Tengblad\, Corey Dalton Hart\, Jason McStoots\, Aaron Sheeha
 n\, Sumner Thompson\, Paul Guttry\, David McFerrin\, Scott Metcalfe\, harp
  & fiddle\, artistic director.\n\nSources: Vermont Public
LOCATION:Cathedral Church of St. Paul\, 2 Cherry Street
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/burlington
 -baroque-festival-bostons-blue-heron-12-09-2026-12-23-28
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Burlington Baroque Festival: Divine Songs: Renaissance Chansons & 
 Motets
DTSTART:20260919T140000
DTEND:20260919T153000
DTSTAMP:20260919T143151Z
UID:6632af03191c047036cf0eb0d7a735@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:BURLINGTON BAROQUE FESTIVAL Thursday\, September 17th thru Sun
 day\, September 20th\, 2026 College Street Congregational Church\, Burling
 ton The Cathedral Church of St. Paul\, Burlington The University of Vermon
 t Recital Hall\, Burlington Burlington Baroque presents five performances 
 featuring internationally acclaimed Artists-in-Residence L’Harmonie des 
 saisons Baroque Orchestra\, Boston’s Blue Heron Renaissance Ensemble\, a
 nd the Burlington Baroque Festival Singers. The Third Annual BURLINGTON BA
 ROQUE FESTIVAL under the direction of Eric Milnes will feature a wondrous 
 array of glorious repertoire offered by a renowned ensemble of specialists
  performing in historically informed style and on the period baroque instr
 uments for which the music was written. Our festival Artists-in-Residence
 \, who are regularly featured in festival performances across North Americ
 a\, Europe\, South America and Asia\, will be gathered in Burlington for t
 he week and will be joined by the Burlington Baroque Festival Singers\, an
 d Boston’s Blue Heron Ensemble for five spectacular performances at thre
 e Burlington venues\, from Thursday\, September 17th through Sunday\, Sept
 ember 20th\, 2026. Don’t miss this opportunity to hear the great reperto
 ire of the Baroque period with an award winning Baroque Orchestra\, intern
 ationally acclaimed vocal soloists and the Burlington Baroque Festival Sin
 gers\, offering listeners a rare opportunity to experience this incredible
  music anew - and from a fresh perspective. Saturday\, September 19th\, 2:
 00 p.m. Divine Song: Renaissance Chansons & Motets Boston’s Blue Heron\,
  Scott Metcalfe\, Director The Cathedral Church of St. Paul\, Burlington A
 dults $40-$80\, $10 Student\, Children free\n\nSources: Vermont Public
LOCATION:Cathedral of Saint Paul\, Burlington\, 2 Cherry St
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/burlington
 -baroque-festival-divine-songs-renaissance-chansons-amp-motets-17-08-2026-
 00-45-18
END:VEVENT
